# The tests read these files as text and the dev server serves them to a browser,
# so keep the same bytes in the working tree as in the object store: text is
# stored as LF and checked out as LF, on every platform. Binaries listed last
# win over the catch-all rule.
* text eol=lf
# Windows batch files are read by cmd.exe, which wants CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.glb binary
*.png binary
# An .ico payload is raw pixels (DIBs for the small sizes) or a compressed PNG
# stream (the large ones); a stray 0D 0A inside either would be eaten by the
# catch-all rule above, the same corruption the reference photo hit once.
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.blend binary
